From: TheMoon <execorvo@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zram: lz4 primary compressor, zstd for idle-page recompression

CONFIG_ZRAM_DEF_COMP_LZ4=y sets lz4 as the primary (hot-path)
compressor, favoring speed over ratio for pages being actively
swapped in/out.

zram_drv.c additionally sets zstd as the ZRAM_MULTI_COMP secondary
compressor: idle/cold pages get recompressed with zstd, trading extra
CPU time for a better ratio -- worth it since those pages are already
infrequently touched by definition.

Applies to:
- kernel-6.6/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
- kernel-6.6/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c (zram_add(), near the
  existing comp_algorithm_set(zram, ZRAM_PRIMARY_COMP, ...) call)
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
index 4e687735adeb..3333333333 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig
@@ -328,6 +328,7 @@ CONFIG_ARM_SCPI_PROTOCOL=y
 # CONFIG_EFI_ARMSTUB_DTB_LOADER is not set
 CONFIG_GNSS=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM=m
+CONFIG_ZRAM_DEF_COMP_LZ4=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM_WRITEBACK=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM_MULTI_COMP=y
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP=y
diff --git a/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c b/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
index 7b2fc33d341e..094a8cd62080 100644
--- a/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
@@ -2249,6 +2249,13 @@ static int zram_add(void)
 	snprintf(zram->disk->disk_name, 16, "zram%d", device_id);

 	comp_algorithm_set(zram, ZRAM_PRIMARY_COMP, default_compressor);
+#ifdef CONFIG_ZRAM_MULTI_COMP
+	/* Default secondary compressor for idle-page recompression: zstd
+	 * trades extra CPU time for a better ratio, which is worth it for
+	 * pages that are cold enough to be recompressed in the first place.
+	 */
+	comp_algorithm_set(zram, ZRAM_SECONDARY_COMP, "zstd");
+#endif

 	/* Actual capacity set using sysfs (/sys/block/zram<id>/disksize */
 	set_capacity(zram->disk, 0);
